WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Press play. Subtitles appear.
200+ languages. One app:  tryray.app

2
00:04:29.637 --> 00:04:31.873
You weren't afraid.
were you. Dix?

3
00:04:39.013 --> 00:04:40.280
Come on.

4
00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:41.516
I want to go see Dad.

5
00:04:48.623 --> 00:04:53.661
<i>Outpost log entry 516. first</i>
<i>week of the new year. '65.</i>

6
00:04:57.832 --> 00:05:00.168
<i>The different set</i>
<i>of handwriting here at the end.</i>

7
00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:03.671
<i>different because this is</i>
<i>my first and last entry</i>

8
00:05:03.805 --> 00:05:06.373
<i>into this logbook.</i>

9
00:05:06.507 --> 00:05:10.111
<i>Major General Edward James</i>
<i>Horn. retired US Army officer</i>

10
00:05:10.244 --> 00:05:15.216
<i>and Pinkerton. is deceased.</i>
<i>four weeks. pneumonia.</i>

11
00:05:16.383 --> 00:05:18.920
<i>buried by his daughter</i>
<i>and only living kin.</i>

12
00:05:19.053 --> 00:05:21.589
<i>Adeline Elizabeth Horn.</i>

13
00:05:21.722 --> 00:05:24.324
<i>The ground was almost</i>
<i>too frozen to dig into.</i>

14
00:05:25.827 --> 00:05:28.262
Watch him ride right by.

15
00:05:28.395 --> 00:05:30.631
You better circle back.

16
00:05:30.765 --> 00:05:32.033
Dig. dig.

17
00:05:37.538 --> 00:05:38.840
Gus.

18
00:05:41.209 --> 00:05:43.077
You little survivor.

19
00:05:43.211 --> 00:05:45.713
Today. circle back.

20
00:05:53.254 --> 00:05:55.323
<i>The outpost will be</i>
<i>abandoned within a day or two</i>

21
00:05:55.455 --> 00:05:59.459
<i>at most. as conditions</i>
<i>have become too harsh.</i>

22
00:05:59.594 --> 00:06:02.930
<i>I've sent letters to Camp Watson</i>
<i>and to the Pinkerton offices</i>

23
00:06:03.064 --> 00:06:05.967
<i>in Chicago requesting</i>
<i>a replacement.</i>

24
00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:07.835
<i>but I've received no word back.</i>

25
00:06:08.836 --> 00:06:10.671
<i>My fear that I have been</i>
<i>forgotten by the world</i>

26
00:06:10.805 --> 00:06:14.842
<i>is overwhelmed</i>
<i>by a deeper fear...</i>

27
00:06:17.311 --> 00:06:19.379
<i>that I was never known at all.</i>

28
00:06:25.553 --> 00:06:27.622
<i>In keeping with my</i>
<i>father's intent.</i>

29
00:06:27.755 --> 00:06:31.259
<i>all supplies will be kept</i>
<i>here. ready and available</i>

30
00:06:31.391 --> 00:06:33.194
<i>for any Union soldier in need.</i>

31
00:06:38.933 --> 00:06:42.904
<i>I'm also leaving this</i>
<i>logbook behind as a marker</i>

32
00:06:45.539 --> 00:06:47.074
<i>that we were here.</i>

33
00:06:50.645 --> 00:06:52.013
<i>Adeline Elizabeth Horn.</i>

34
00:07:18.873 --> 00:07:20.708
<i>I don't know how</i>
<i>I'll earn my way.</i>

35
00:07:20.841 --> 00:07:23.577
<i>and I know that I am letting</i>
<i>my father down by leaving.</i>

36
00:07:24.178 --> 00:07:26.547
<i>I am not the caretaker he was.</i>

37
00:07:27.882 --> 00:07:31.986
<i>I saw a man today.</i>
<i>a soul lost to the wilderness.</i>

38
00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:35.289
<i>and I did not call out</i>
<i>to help him.</i>

39
00:09:02.643 --> 00:09:04.245
Put that light out!

40
00:09:08.182 --> 00:09:12.119
I said. put that thing out.

41
00:09:12.453 --> 00:09:15.723
unless'n you want to get us
both killed.

42
00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:23.998
Where are you keeping
your daddy's garments?

43
00:09:24.131 --> 00:09:25.433
Come on. girlie.

44
00:09:25.566 --> 00:09:27.968
I know you ain't here
by your lonesome.

45
00:09:28.102 --> 00:09:30.171
Come on. out with it.

46
00:09:30.304 --> 00:09:31.972
Bedroom dresser.

47
00:09:32.106 --> 00:09:35.176
Bedroom dresser.

48
00:09:35.309 --> 00:09:37.011
Wait now.

49
00:09:37.144 --> 00:09:38.779
How old?

50
00:09:38.913 --> 00:09:41.348
First thing's gon' be first.

51
00:09:43.084 --> 00:09:44.618
Come over here.

52
00:09:46.521 --> 00:09:47.655
Sit down.

53
00:09:47.788 --> 00:09:49.090
We don't have any money.

54
00:09:49.223 --> 00:09:54.862
Well. that's what
they call an assumption.

55
00:09:56.063 --> 00:09:58.866
But we do have plenty
of food and water. medicine.

56
00:10:00.801 --> 00:10:02.336
You don't need a gun.

57
00:10:04.638 --> 00:10:06.407
My father has had
Army medical training

58
00:10:06.541 --> 00:10:09.443
and should be returning from
his midnight walk presently.

59
00:10:09.877 --> 00:10:13.380
As for me. I know a great deal
about nursing and dressing.

60
00:10:13.515 --> 00:10:14.915
I bandaged myself today.

61
00:10:15.049 --> 00:10:17.519
Bah. foolishness.

62
00:10:18.018 --> 00:10:19.987
Midnight walk.

63
00:10:20.121 --> 00:10:22.790
Get over here and
bring that chair.

64
00:10:32.066 --> 00:10:33.634
You said you weren't
gonna do nothing to me.

65
00:10:33.767 --> 00:10:34.835
Darn right.

66
00:10:34.969 --> 00:10:36.470
Oh. you'll be safe.

67
00:10:37.805 --> 00:10:39.073
I'm a bunny rabbit.

68
00:10:42.009 --> 00:10:44.613
You've got no cause to
tie me up and bully me.

69
00:10:44.745 --> 00:10:46.180
I've told you.

70
00:10:47.248 --> 00:10:52.887
I saw this camp 100
yards out. like an oasis

71
00:10:53.053 --> 00:10:58.359
right there in the
middle of wild nowhere.

72
00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:00.494
Open.

73
00:11:06.267 --> 00:11:07.334
Nothing.

74
00:11:07.468 --> 00:11:08.736
Oh. figures.

75
00:11:11.438 --> 00:11:13.174
Oh. my.

76
00:11:14.643 --> 00:11:17.378
Oh. now this is warmth.

77
00:11:17.512 --> 00:11:19.113
Tell you what.

78
00:11:23.417 --> 00:11:24.485
Look at old Perry.

79
00:11:25.886 --> 00:11:26.987
That's my father's coat.

80
00:11:27.121 --> 00:11:30.457
Oh. he won't mind none.

81
00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:33.027
Gon' be cold.

82
00:11:33.160 --> 00:11:34.361
He's going to track you down

83
00:11:34.495 --> 00:11:36.163
after I tell him
what you did to me.

84
00:11:36.297 --> 00:11:38.966
though I was
unarmed and offered assistance.

85
00:11:39.099 --> 00:11:41.135
Well. you go
right ahead. girlie.

86
00:11:41.268 --> 00:11:44.004
It ain't your daddy
I'm 'fraid of.

87
00:11:47.274 --> 00:11:48.909
Barlow.

88
00:11:49.544 --> 00:11:51.212
Yeah.

89
00:11:53.548 --> 00:11:55.416
Go west. Perry.

90
00:11:55.550 --> 00:11:58.052
Watch him ride right by.

91
00:11:58.185 --> 00:12:00.955
You better circle back.

92
00:12:01.088 --> 00:12:02.256
Dig. dig.

93
00:12:02.389 --> 00:12:03.757
So long. girlie.

94
00:12:03.891 --> 00:12:06.327
Wait. you can't
leave me like this.

95
00:12:06.460 --> 00:12:09.096
Your daddy will
untie you upon his return.

96
00:12:09.230 --> 00:12:10.297
I lied.

97
00:12:10.431 --> 00:12:12.166
No one's coming to find me.

98
00:12:12.299 --> 00:12:13.734
It's just me here.

99
00:12:13.867 --> 00:12:16.638
I don't mind you taking
the clothes or the bread

100
00:12:16.770 --> 00:12:18.005
or the liquor.

101
00:12:18.640 --> 00:12:20.841
but you can't leave me
like this.

102
00:12:21.208 --> 00:12:25.580
tied to a chair.
left to die like a fool.

103
00:12:27.915 --> 00:12:30.217
Just you?

104
00:12:30.351 --> 00:12:31.620
Yes. sir.

105
00:12:33.555 --> 00:12:35.155
I won't cause you no trouble.

106
00:12:35.289 --> 00:12:36.725
You have my word.

107
00:12:41.128 --> 00:12:44.865
Listen. girlie.
he's on his way now.

108
00:12:44.999 --> 00:12:48.469
He don't sleep.
so I don't either.

109
00:12:48.603 --> 00:12:52.373
Wish I could wish you nice.
but the rain coming my way

110
00:12:52.507 --> 00:12:54.041
won't fall on you none.

111
00:13:43.957 --> 00:13:46.493
<i>Watch him ride right by.</i>

112
00:13:46.628 --> 00:13:48.763
<i>Circle back.</i>

113
00:13:48.896 --> 00:13:50.297
<i>Dig. dig.</i>

114
00:14:02.644 --> 00:14:07.014
Colonel. you are faced
with an inevitability.

115
00:14:14.054 --> 00:14:16.957
You will die on this mountain.

116
00:14:19.893 --> 00:14:24.532
I've ordered my men to toss
your regiment into the river.

117
00:14:24.666 --> 00:14:27.569
and your blood will
saturate these woods.

118
00:14:32.774 --> 00:14:35.109
It was a cowardly
surprise attack.

119
00:14:37.579 --> 00:14:40.849
I'm looking for a
man. goes by the name

120
00:14:40.981 --> 00:14:43.016
of Burial Perry Parker.

121
00:14:47.187 --> 00:14:50.324
I don't know this man. Parker.

122
00:14:51.959 --> 00:14:54.928
That is not what
I was hoping to hear.

123
00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:13.782
What do
you think. Dixie?

124
00:17:08.796 --> 00:17:11.966
I fear I am dead in this place
without this gold. so I took it.

125
00:17:12.499 --> 00:17:14.002
Do not judge me.

126
00:17:14.134 --> 00:17:16.738
You raised me well enough. but
you have not been where I am.

127
00:17:17.471 --> 00:17:19.406
I'll say goodbye
to you both. and I

128
00:17:19.541 --> 00:17:22.777
will start my journey
southwest to the settlers road

129
00:17:22.911 --> 00:17:24.378
and then on to Astoria.

130
00:17:25.412 --> 00:17:26.948
I cannot bring you with me.

131
00:17:30.018 --> 00:17:33.988
But I love you. and I will
return for your portraits

132
00:17:34.121 --> 00:17:36.958
one day when I am no longer
fearful of being hunted.

133
00:17:44.431 --> 00:17:46.500
♪ <i>For mine eyes</i>
<i>have seen the glory</i> ♪

134
00:17:46.634 --> 00:17:49.169
♪ <i>of the coming of the Lord</i> ♪

135
00:17:49.303 --> 00:17:51.906
♪ <i>He's trampling out the</i>
<i>vintage where the grapes</i> ♪

136
00:17:52.040 --> 00:17:54.709
♪ <i>of wrath are stored</i> ♪

137
00:17:54.842 --> 00:17:59.914
♪ <i>His truth is marching on</i> ♪

138
00:18:01.683 --> 00:18:03.450
♪ <i>Mine eyes</i>
<i>Have seen the glory</i> ♪

139
00:18:03.585 --> 00:18:05.954
♪ <i>of the coming of the Lord</i> ♪

140
00:18:54.769 --> 00:18:56.004
Come on.

141
00:18:56.136 --> 00:18:57.404
We both have to
do our fair share.

142
00:19:28.036 --> 00:19:29.336
Shot to pieces.

143
00:19:53.393 --> 00:19:55.096
Oh. my goodness.

144
00:20:02.503 --> 00:20:03.838
You're alive.

145
00:20:04.337 --> 00:20:05.740
But you won't be for
much longer out here.

146
00:20:20.188 --> 00:20:22.924
It don't look deserted.

147
00:20:23.057 --> 00:20:24.424
Sure ain't.

148
00:20:58.059 --> 00:20:59.794
Edward Horn.

149
00:21:18.179 --> 00:21:19.412
They are Union.

150
00:21:21.582 --> 00:21:22.850
We're safe.

151
00:21:33.493 --> 00:21:35.328
Is this woman in
your party. soldier?

152
00:21:36.296 --> 00:21:37.665
I'll be damned.

153
00:21:38.398 --> 00:21:39.499
Colonel!

154
00:21:46.274 --> 00:21:49.577
You are the
caretaker's daughter?

155
00:21:49.710 --> 00:21:50.778
Yes. sir.

156
00:21:50.912 --> 00:21:52.013
Ada.

157
00:21:52.146 --> 00:21:54.882
We have been anticipating you.

158
00:21:55.016 --> 00:21:58.719
Colonel John Good. Cavalry
Company G. Camp Watson.

159
00:21:58.853 --> 00:22:00.588
Camp Watson?

160
00:22:00.721 --> 00:22:01.789
Oh. thank God for you. Colonel.

161
00:22:01.923 --> 00:22:03.591
You received my letters.

162
00:22:05.392 --> 00:22:08.095
Do not let my
lieutenant here scare you.

163
00:22:08.229 --> 00:22:11.265
I'm certain he's the first
full-blooded red paint

164
00:22:11.398 --> 00:22:12.800
you've seen.

165
00:22:12.934 --> 00:22:15.570
But he's a man for the
Union. same as you or I.

166
00:22:15.703 --> 00:22:18.973
I saw the Union blue. sir.

167
00:22:19.106 --> 00:22:23.744
Your logbook informs me
that your warden has passed.

168
00:22:24.879 --> 00:22:26.446
It's been four weeks.

169
00:22:27.315 --> 00:22:29.183
My condolences.

170
00:22:30.952 --> 00:22:32.653
Your hand is injured.

171
00:22:32.787 --> 00:22:34.387
I had a misfire.

172
00:22:34.522 --> 00:22:35.723
My. you were shooting?

173
00:22:36.524 --> 00:22:37.457
Yes. sir.

174
00:22:40.328 --> 00:22:42.330
Who was the lucky target?

175
00:22:43.664 --> 00:22:44.932
Wolves.

176
00:22:47.602 --> 00:22:49.303
Dry clothes. miss?

177
00:22:49.837 --> 00:22:51.138
Plenty.

178
00:22:51.471 --> 00:22:54.709
Bring some socks and
all the blankets you've got.

179
00:22:56.744 --> 00:22:59.714
Miss Horn. you were
equipped with a Franklin.

180
00:22:59.847 --> 00:23:00.915
Yes. sir.

181
00:23:01.048 --> 00:23:02.783
I'd appreciate some coffee.

182
00:23:02.917 --> 00:23:05.452
It's been a month
since I had a cup.

183
00:23:06.187 --> 00:23:06.988
I'll brew some.

184
00:23:07.121 --> 00:23:08.222
Thank you.

185
00:24:03.811 --> 00:24:07.548
Miss Horn. where's my coffee?

186
00:24:07.682 --> 00:24:09.817
Oh. brewing. Colonel.

187
00:24:14.922 --> 00:24:15.990
Will she be OK. Colonel?

188
00:24:16.123 --> 00:24:17.425
She'll be fine.

189
00:24:20.261 --> 00:24:24.699
I'm sure you've noticed we've
taken your Hawken rifle.

190
00:24:24.832 --> 00:24:27.868
I apologize. but it's
a safety precaution.

191
00:24:28.002 --> 00:24:29.737
You understand?

192
00:24:29.870 --> 00:24:32.873
It's broken. so no matter.

193
00:24:33.007 --> 00:24:36.344
I'll have Sergeant Baker
see if he can't repair it.

194
00:24:40.982 --> 00:24:41.882
Colonel.

195
00:24:44.285 --> 00:24:48.789
Miss Horn. we have what you
might call a delicate situation

196
00:24:48.923 --> 00:24:50.725
on our hands.

197
00:24:50.858 --> 00:24:54.362
I have a prisoner under my
guard that needs dealing with.

198
00:24:54.494 --> 00:24:55.596
Red!

199
00:24:55.730 --> 00:24:56.864
Red. look at me go!

200
00:24:56.998 --> 00:24:58.299
Whoo!

201
00:24:58.432 --> 00:24:59.533
I'm flying!

202
00:24:59.667 --> 00:25:01.802
He's a dangerous man.

203
00:25:05.272 --> 00:25:07.508
A thief.

204
00:25:07.641 --> 00:25:10.845
Of course. you would not have
to be bothered by any of this.

205
00:25:10.978 --> 00:25:13.581
except that it's over
four days' hard travel

206
00:25:13.714 --> 00:25:15.783
down this mountain
to Camp Watson.

207
00:25:16.917 --> 00:25:18.919
If this man is a
thief. Colonel. then he

208
00:25:19.053 --> 00:25:21.355
should be dealt with
rightly by the court of law.

209
00:25:21.489 --> 00:25:23.724
In times of peace and
civility. you would be right.

210
00:25:23.858 --> 00:25:25.092
Miss Horn.

211
00:25:25.226 --> 00:25:28.195
But these are
extraordinary times.

212
00:25:28.329 --> 00:25:30.031
Colonel!

213
00:25:30.164 --> 00:25:32.366
Come. then.

214
00:25:32.500 --> 00:25:33.734
Join us.

215
00:25:41.208 --> 00:25:42.376
Girlie!

216
00:25:42.511 --> 00:25:44.345
Oh. thank Jesus.

217
00:25:44.478 --> 00:25:47.581
Will you tell Fiddler
that I had nothing on me?

218
00:25:47.715 --> 00:25:49.617
Nothing on me at all!

219
00:25:49.750 --> 00:25:50.885
Tell him!

220
00:25:52.586 --> 00:25:55.990
Ada. this here
is Private CE Caldwell.

221
00:25:56.123 --> 00:25:58.826
Miss Horn was kind
enough to return Miss

222
00:25:58.959 --> 00:26:01.629
Emily to us safe and sound.

223
00:26:01.762 --> 00:26:02.830
Comin' in.

224
00:26:02.963 --> 00:26:04.665
Pleasure.

225
00:26:04.799 --> 00:26:07.868
And this here
is Sergeant Baker.

226
00:26:08.002 --> 00:26:09.070
You can call me Red.

227
00:26:10.104 --> 00:26:11.806
Pleased to meet you both.

228
00:26:11.939 --> 00:26:13.841
Well. girlie.
now that you've

229
00:26:13.974 --> 00:26:17.411
met everyone all
cordial and mannerly.

230
00:26:17.546 --> 00:26:22.551
will you please tell these
gentlemen I had nothing on me?

231
00:26:22.683 --> 00:26:24.285
She heard you. Perry.

232
00:26:25.086 --> 00:26:27.922
Please do not
interrupt me again.

233
00:26:28.055 --> 00:26:31.258
Have you seen this man before?

234
00:26:31.392 --> 00:26:32.660
Yes. sir.

235
00:26:32.793 --> 00:26:34.261
He was in the cabin
two nights ago.

236
00:26:34.395 --> 00:26:37.431
I-- I was just looking
for food and spirits.

237
00:26:37.566 --> 00:26:39.100
I swear. Fiddler.

238
00:26:40.768 --> 00:26:42.803
He's not lying. Colonel.

239
00:26:42.937 --> 00:26:44.004
He didn't have nothing on him.

240
00:26:44.138 --> 00:26:45.639
Nothing that I saw.

241
00:26:45.773 --> 00:26:47.374
He was just in need of
bread and some whiskey.

242
00:26:47.509 --> 00:26:49.110
And he stole nothing from you?

243
00:26:49.243 --> 00:26:50.411
No. sir.

244
00:26:50.545 --> 00:26:51.846
No. sir.

245
00:26:51.979 --> 00:26:53.047
No.

246
00:26:53.180 --> 00:26:54.915
No.

247
00:26:55.049 --> 00:26:58.553
The Chesterfield he's
wearing is my father's. and I'd

248
00:26:58.686 --> 00:27:01.055
like it back.

249
00:27:01.188 --> 00:27:02.256
Yeah.

250
00:27:02.389 --> 00:27:05.826
No. no. no. no. no. no.

251
00:27:05.960 --> 00:27:09.196
The man presently hanging
off your barn rafter

252
00:27:09.330 --> 00:27:11.365
is Burial Perry Parker.

253
00:27:11.499 --> 00:27:15.169
I know him well. and
I'm not fond of him.

254
00:27:15.302 --> 00:27:17.705
He's a grave robber and a thief.

255
00:27:17.838 --> 00:27:21.342
He has something
that belongs to me.

256
00:27:21.475 --> 00:27:24.546
But he wouldn't have
the item on him.

257
00:27:24.678 --> 00:27:28.415
It would be buried
in these woods.

258
00:27:37.592 --> 00:27:38.659
Colonel--

259
00:27:54.375 --> 00:27:57.111
Thank you. Sergeant.

260
00:27:57.244 --> 00:28:00.247
Saddle up the horses.

261
00:28:00.381 --> 00:28:02.016
We'll see where he takes us.

262
00:28:05.620 --> 00:28:09.223
I'm sorry that you had
to see that. Miss Horn.

263
00:28:09.356 --> 00:28:11.792
I hope you'll forgive
us the intrusion.

264
00:28:11.926 --> 00:28:13.662
Looks like we'll
be here overnight.

265
00:28:13.794 --> 00:28:15.462
But don't you worry.

266
00:28:15.597 --> 00:28:19.500
My men are happy to chew on
hardtack in the barn here.

267
00:28:19.634 --> 00:28:21.402
so we'll be of no bother.

268
00:28:21.536 --> 00:28:23.971
No.

269
00:28:24.104 --> 00:28:25.739
I'll have supper ready for you
and your men

270
00:28:25.873 --> 00:28:27.241
in the cabin shortly.

271
00:28:27.374 --> 00:28:29.210
Why. thank you. Miss Horn.

272
00:28:31.845 --> 00:28:32.846
It's Ada.

273
00:28:36.016 --> 00:28:37.751
Ada.

274
00:29:21.996 --> 00:29:23.297
Untie him.

275
00:29:37.144 --> 00:29:38.445
Dig.

276
00:30:34.001 --> 00:30:35.069
Perry.

277
00:30:52.252 --> 00:30:53.487
That sumbitch.

278
00:30:57.525 --> 00:31:00.494
Come to give us a hand. kid?

279
00:31:00.628 --> 00:31:02.630
Ground's frozen solid.

280
00:31:02.764 --> 00:31:04.833
Winter around here
ain't a good time

281
00:31:04.965 --> 00:31:08.001
for a man to meet his end.

282
00:31:08.135 --> 00:31:09.637
You end up with no
place to put him.

283
00:31:12.774 --> 00:31:16.210
The. uh. colonel
know you're here?

284
00:31:16.343 --> 00:31:19.012
That man has my father's
coat and his Wellington boots.

285
00:31:25.386 --> 00:31:26.887
First time
seeing one. kid?

286
00:31:29.957 --> 00:31:30.991
No.

287
00:31:36.897 --> 00:31:38.165
Hey. girl!

288
00:31:38.298 --> 00:31:41.636
Ain't proper to bury a man
in no footwear whatsoever!

289
00:31:41.770 --> 00:31:44.905
Man's gotta have the things
he needs going across.

290
00:31:45.038 --> 00:31:46.808
I'm not the one
decided to shoot him.

291
00:31:58.787 --> 00:31:59.953
Here.

292
00:32:00.087 --> 00:32:02.657
Your turn.

293
00:32:47.100 --> 00:32:51.205
Emily. go and introduce
yourself to Miss Horn.

294
00:32:51.338 --> 00:32:54.074
and bring that salt pork
to the supper table.

295
00:33:00.915 --> 00:33:03.651
I can take these here plates.

296
00:33:03.785 --> 00:33:05.920
Here.

297
00:33:06.053 --> 00:33:07.956
I'm glad to see
you're up and about.

298
00:33:08.121 --> 00:33:10.057
You'll let me know
if you need anything.

299
00:33:10.190 --> 00:33:11.659
We're a fully stocked outpost.

300
00:33:16.063 --> 00:33:17.264
While it's steaming!

301
00:33:20.702 --> 00:33:22.504
You brought me here?

302
00:33:22.637 --> 00:33:26.808
It was luck and clumsiness.

303
00:33:26.941 --> 00:33:28.543
Well. I don't figure
I owe you nothing.

304
00:33:28.676 --> 00:33:29.944
if that's what you think.

305
00:33:39.253 --> 00:33:41.956
Can't say I ever let
a whore eat before me.

306
00:33:42.356 --> 00:33:44.692
Whore is further up the
food chain than scoundrel.

307
00:33:47.127 --> 00:33:49.129
You've got a mouth on you.

308
00:33:49.263 --> 00:33:50.364
I thank you. Ada.

309
00:33:50.497 --> 00:33:52.266
Thanks. kid.

310
00:33:52.399 --> 00:33:53.902
Since you've
been kind enough

311
00:33:54.034 --> 00:33:57.404
to take us into your home.
I thought you might do

312
00:33:57.539 --> 00:33:59.641
us the honor of saying grace.

313
00:33:59.774 --> 00:34:01.074
Grace?

314
00:34:01.208 --> 00:34:03.912
A blessing for the food.

315
00:34:04.044 --> 00:34:05.780
I'm afraid I don't
know it. Colonel.

316
00:34:05.914 --> 00:34:09.283
You don't need
anything prepared. Ada.

317
00:34:09.416 --> 00:34:13.655
But if you were feeling shy--

318
00:34:17.759 --> 00:34:19.928
I'm not shy.

319
00:34:20.060 --> 00:34:21.829
I know the prayer my
father used to say.

320
00:34:21.963 --> 00:34:23.330
Well. let's hear it. then.

321
00:34:34.809 --> 00:34:36.778
Give us the
strength. good Lord.

322
00:34:36.911 --> 00:34:38.846
to set the world at naught.

323
00:34:39.714 --> 00:34:41.348
so that we may make a cry
unto Thee

324
00:34:41.481 --> 00:34:43.417
in this hour
of our country's need.

325
00:34:46.621 --> 00:34:51.391
Deal with us not by our
sins or our misdeeds.

326
00:34:52.492 --> 00:34:55.128
but reach forth with Your
right hand and be our defense.

327
00:34:57.832 --> 00:34:59.534
Have pity on our
brothers in arms

328
00:34:59.667 --> 00:35:02.804
who are against the
authority of the land.

329
00:35:02.937 --> 00:35:05.372
and allow them to see
the error of their ways.

330
00:35:08.509 --> 00:35:13.413
Last. allow us to bear the
weight of the grief of those

331
00:35:13.548 --> 00:35:15.215
we have known and loved.

332
00:35:18.620 --> 00:35:23.725
And for those we do not know who
have passed on into the unknown.

333
00:35:25.827 --> 00:35:30.665
we will remember always in
our silence and in our dreams.

334
00:35:35.003 --> 00:35:36.303
Amen.

335
00:35:36.436 --> 00:35:37.839
Amen.

336
00:35:37.972 --> 00:35:40.307
Well. God damn.

337
00:35:40.440 --> 00:35:42.442
I need a drink after that one.

338
00:35:45.379 --> 00:35:48.082
We've got a full-blooded
Union loyalist. Colonel.

339
00:35:48.215 --> 00:35:49.517
Drink up. kid.

340
00:35:55.723 --> 00:35:57.925
Looks like we came
to the right place.

341
00:36:06.968 --> 00:36:09.971
I don't pretend to know
more about the war than I do.

342
00:36:10.104 --> 00:36:11.839
We are remote.

343
00:36:11.973 --> 00:36:13.841
Though. a fur trader did
come through here on his way

344
00:36:13.975 --> 00:36:15.442
to the Columbia River.

345
00:36:15.576 --> 00:36:19.947
He had a February 5.
1862 <i>New York Tribune.</i>

346
00:36:20.081 --> 00:36:22.784
He let me read it
through before he left.

347
00:36:22.917 --> 00:36:24.585
What'd you gather from it?

348
00:36:24.719 --> 00:36:29.289
Well. for one. the Yankee
paper's full of advertisements.

349
00:36:29.423 --> 00:36:32.160
And I'd very much like to
see a live hippopotamus

350
00:36:32.292 --> 00:36:35.697
from the Barnum Museum. and the
Commodore Nutt. who apparently

351
00:36:35.830 --> 00:36:39.033
is the world's smallest man.

352
00:36:39.167 --> 00:36:41.969
Him and the hippopotamuses
I'd like to see.

353
00:36:45.039 --> 00:36:49.276
Though if what I saw today is
even a splinter of the war.

354
00:36:49.409 --> 00:36:51.411
then I'm grateful to
not have taken part.

355
00:36:57.919 --> 00:37:00.555
My punishment was too severe?

356
00:37:04.859 --> 00:37:07.528
No. of course not.

357
00:37:08.328 --> 00:37:09.296
Forgive me.

358
00:37:09.429 --> 00:37:11.599
This is the most
I've spoken in weeks.

359
00:37:12.734 --> 00:37:15.803
Your-- your daddy is passed?

360
00:37:15.937 --> 00:37:17.505
He is dead.

361
00:37:17.638 --> 00:37:19.507
Poor Daddy brought you up
on this godforsaken mountain

362
00:37:19.640 --> 00:37:21.374
for what. swine husbandry?

363
00:37:21.509 --> 00:37:24.746
I mean. God damn it. that
don't make one lick of sense.

364
00:37:24.879 --> 00:37:26.781
Every man follows
his own path.

365
00:37:26.914 --> 00:37:29.183
I mean. yeah. but her dad do
sound like a bit of a loon-o.

366
00:37:29.316 --> 00:37:30.785
don't he?

367
00:37:30.918 --> 00:37:35.056
Rob. that whiskey's gone
and soiled your etiquette.

368
00:37:35.823 --> 00:37:38.993
My father was an operative
under Allan Pinkerton. sir.

369
00:37:39.127 --> 00:37:41.796
That plaque in there. he
received upon his retirement

370
00:37:41.929 --> 00:37:43.798
for a commendation
of excellence.

371
00:37:46.466 --> 00:37:49.871
Not long after. we boarded the
<i>SS Antelope</i> at the Pacific wharf

372
00:37:50.004 --> 00:37:53.875
in San Francisco. though
I remember none of it.

373
00:37:54.008 --> 00:37:55.777
I was too young.

374
00:37:55.910 --> 00:37:59.580
Caught sight of some gray
wolves out there. runt.

375
00:37:59.714 --> 00:38:01.949
A few more than
I'd like to count.

376
00:38:02.083 --> 00:38:05.318
Looks like they'll be knocking
on your door soon. missy.

377
00:38:05.452 --> 00:38:07.088
Gotta move them hogs.

378
00:38:07.221 --> 00:38:08.355
That sow's got pneumonia.

379
00:38:08.488 --> 00:38:10.224
She's going to pass soon.

380
00:38:11.793 --> 00:38:13.694
I'm leaving here anyhow.

381
00:38:13.828 --> 00:38:16.164
I'm going to California.

382
00:38:16.296 --> 00:38:19.100
The gold rush is dead. Ada.

383
00:38:19.233 --> 00:38:21.235
I'm surprised the news
ain't traveled to you.

384
00:38:21.368 --> 00:38:24.404
It's been quite some time.

385
00:38:24.539 --> 00:38:26.073
I'm not interested in gold.

386
00:38:30.343 --> 00:38:33.748
Everyone is
interested in gold. Ada.

387
00:38:33.881 --> 00:38:35.783
No. sir.

388
00:38:35.917 --> 00:38:37.985
My mother is from San Francisco.

389
00:38:38.119 --> 00:38:40.721
I figured I have some
family down that way.

390
00:38:40.855 --> 00:38:43.456
She's looking
to travel. Colonel.

391
00:38:43.591 --> 00:38:46.160
See a hippopotamus or two.

392
00:38:46.294 --> 00:38:47.427
Two would be something.

393
00:38:50.497 --> 00:38:53.668
I don't reckon I'd like to be
stuck out here by my lonesome

394
00:38:53.801 --> 00:38:55.069
neither.

395
00:38:55.203 --> 00:38:56.737
No. sir.

396
00:38:56.871 --> 00:38:58.973
We will be out
of your way soon.

397
00:38:59.106 --> 00:39:02.677
We have business in these woods.

398
00:39:02.810 --> 00:39:05.112
It should be
settled by tomorrow.

399
00:39:05.246 --> 00:39:08.883
Even faster with your
help. if you don't

400
00:39:09.016 --> 00:39:12.053
mind joining our expedition.

401
00:39:12.186 --> 00:39:14.088
You know these woods
better than anyone.

402
00:39:14.222 --> 00:39:16.157
Isn't that right?

403
00:39:16.290 --> 00:39:18.326
Yes. sir.

404
00:39:18.458 --> 00:39:22.763
As soon as our
business is finished.

405
00:39:22.897 --> 00:39:24.431
we will leave you in peace.

406
00:39:51.592 --> 00:39:54.295
It was foolish to kill him.

407
00:39:54.427 --> 00:39:56.197
Perry was a born liar.

408
00:39:56.330 --> 00:39:58.366
Lied right till his last breath.

409
00:39:58.498 --> 00:40:01.569
He was never going
to give up that gold.

410
00:40:01.702 --> 00:40:03.304
What if he wasn't lying?

411
00:40:03.436 --> 00:40:07.642
That the gold he stole
from me was stolen from him?

412
00:40:07.775 --> 00:40:10.077
Burial could have told
her to move it for a cut.

413
00:40:10.211 --> 00:40:11.712
Then where is it. Charlie?

414
00:40:11.846 --> 00:40:14.447
You went over this
outpost same as me.

415
00:40:14.582 --> 00:40:17.051
I seen no place it's
been buried or hung.

416
00:40:17.184 --> 00:40:18.586
It ain't up in no God damn tree.

417
00:40:18.719 --> 00:40:19.654
Yee-ha!

418
00:40:24.959 --> 00:40:26.127
Yee-ha!

419
00:40:26.260 --> 00:40:27.328
Woo!

420
00:40:46.080 --> 00:40:47.949
That's it.

421
00:40:52.420 --> 00:40:56.157
Is your private not riding
with us this morning. Colonel?

422
00:40:56.290 --> 00:40:59.360
He is sleeping off a headache.

423
00:40:59.492 --> 00:41:02.096
Well. I've medicine
for that. Colonel.

424
00:41:02.229 --> 00:41:05.433
I bet you do. Ada.

425
00:41:10.204 --> 00:41:13.207
How much do you
know about tracking?

426
00:41:13.341 --> 00:41:15.710
I know the difference
between wolf and rabbit tracks.

427
00:41:15.843 --> 00:41:20.181
I figured. since
your daddy was Pinkerton.

428
00:41:20.314 --> 00:41:22.516
My lessons were cut short.

429
00:41:22.650 --> 00:41:24.118
You said you'd
been fishing when

430
00:41:24.251 --> 00:41:26.153
you returned to the outpost.

431
00:41:26.287 --> 00:41:27.655
Tried to.

432
00:41:27.788 --> 00:41:29.489
I camped on the way
to my favorite spot.

433
00:41:29.623 --> 00:41:31.158
a bend in the river.
where the steelhead

434
00:41:31.292 --> 00:41:33.461
get caught in a whirlpool.

435
00:41:33.594 --> 00:41:35.997
I found Ms. Emily before
I could sink my line.

436
00:41:36.130 --> 00:41:38.933
And you heard nothing
of our firefight?

437
00:41:39.066 --> 00:41:40.968
I heard your
melee from a distance.

438
00:41:41.102 --> 00:41:43.804
though. I was too scared
to move on in the morning.

439
00:41:43.938 --> 00:41:46.741
But you did continue.

440
00:41:46.874 --> 00:41:50.244
Hunger beats fear.

441
00:41:53.214 --> 00:41:56.217
Keep your eyes to the ground.

442
00:41:56.350 --> 00:41:58.319
Fresh tracks will show wet.

443
00:41:58.452 --> 00:42:00.955
And the ground's been turned up.

444
00:42:01.088 --> 00:42:03.257
Best thing we can
do is to start where

445
00:42:03.391 --> 00:42:06.527
we found him. go from there.

446
00:42:09.497 --> 00:42:12.266
You'll show me this
bend in the river.

447
00:42:12.400 --> 00:42:13.467
Yes. sir.

448
00:42:19.040 --> 00:42:22.009
Is that Father
and Mother Horn?

449
00:42:22.143 --> 00:42:26.180
My father took great care
of making my mother's cross.

450
00:42:26.313 --> 00:42:29.250
The cross I made for
him does not compare.

451
00:42:29.383 --> 00:42:33.954
No. it does not.

452
00:42:34.955 --> 00:42:36.891
We will make sure to
visit them properly

453
00:42:37.024 --> 00:42:40.694
before we leave.
pay our respects.

454
00:43:20.601 --> 00:43:22.236
Still feeling
low. Ms. Emily?

455
00:43:26.340 --> 00:43:28.510
You mean from you
leaving me to drown?

456
00:43:28.642 --> 00:43:30.678
I was
supposed to shoot you.

457
00:43:30.811 --> 00:43:33.013
It was Mr. Fiddler's orders.

458
00:43:33.147 --> 00:43:34.615
But you didn't.

459
00:43:34.748 --> 00:43:36.784
No. I shot your mare
instead. gave you a chance.

460
00:43:37.519 --> 00:43:38.919
Mr. Perry showing up
gave you good cover.

461
00:43:39.053 --> 00:43:42.591
but you weren't
supposed to reappear.

462
00:43:42.756 --> 00:43:46.528
Is that what
you're here for now?

463
00:43:46.660 --> 00:43:48.662
No.

464
00:43:48.796 --> 00:43:50.364
Fiddler done changed his mind.

465
00:43:52.900 --> 00:43:54.668
But I think I'll still give
you that punishment. though.

466
00:44:05.846 --> 00:44:06.881
Whoa.

467
00:44:15.624 --> 00:44:17.258
She was here.

468
00:44:17.391 --> 00:44:20.694
Once your officer is
through checking my story.

469
00:44:20.828 --> 00:44:22.830
there's a lookout point
not far from here.

470
00:44:22.963 --> 00:44:23.998
I must show you.

471
00:44:24.131 --> 00:44:25.833
It really is something.

472
00:44:25.966 --> 00:44:28.369
You just gonna keep
letting her mouth off like that?

473
00:44:28.502 --> 00:44:30.037
What would you have me do?

474
00:44:30.171 --> 00:44:32.673
I believe this young
lady has taken over

475
00:44:32.806 --> 00:44:34.708
as leader of this expedition.

476
00:44:44.952 --> 00:44:46.621
This map is full of
inaccuracies. Colonel.

477
00:44:46.754 --> 00:44:50.024
It's no wonder you're lost.

478
00:44:50.157 --> 00:44:52.594
We're not lost.

479
00:44:52.726 --> 00:44:54.328
Well. whatever it
is you have lost.

480
00:44:54.461 --> 00:44:55.996
you'll not find
it with this map.

481
00:44:56.497 --> 00:44:58.600
Camp Watson is not
south as it says here.

482
00:44:58.732 --> 00:45:01.168
but it's directly east
through the high pines

483
00:45:01.302 --> 00:45:03.971
for a day and a half until
you reach the Grass Valley.

484
00:45:04.104 --> 00:45:06.508
And then it is south for
another two days along the fur

485
00:45:06.641 --> 00:45:07.708
traders' path.

486
00:45:07.841 --> 00:45:09.410
I drew that map. girl.

487
00:45:09.544 --> 00:45:11.212
Well. then. you're not such
a great red paint tracker

488
00:45:11.345 --> 00:45:13.180
after all.
Red:

489
00:45:13.582 --> 00:45:14.848
I reckon your
navigator should at least

490
00:45:14.982 --> 00:45:17.251
know where you come from.

491
00:45:17.384 --> 00:45:19.654
I'll be happy to replace
him as a part of your outfit

492
00:45:19.787 --> 00:45:21.088
if your pay is up to snuff.

493
00:45:26.460 --> 00:45:28.530
Now. if you'll
excuse me. Colonel. I

494
00:45:28.663 --> 00:45:30.699
have to kill an animal
that is very dear to me.

495
00:45:30.831 --> 00:45:33.367
And I don't need no one around.

496
00:45:33.500 --> 00:45:35.836
It's a private matter.

497
00:45:35.970 --> 00:45:37.204
Go on then.

498
00:45:40.441 --> 00:45:43.377
Good Lord. that girl's got
a sass on her. don't she?

499
00:45:46.013 --> 00:45:48.082
I'm growing fond of that sass.

500
00:46:34.295 --> 00:46:35.362
Get off of her!

501
00:46:35.496 --> 00:46:36.765
What the fuck?

502
00:46:36.897 --> 00:46:38.365
Ma'am. are you OK?
What did he do--

503
00:46:38.499 --> 00:46:39.634
I'm OK. Ada.

504
00:46:39.768 --> 00:46:41.201
What the fuck you
think you're doing. girl?

505
00:46:41.335 --> 00:46:42.870
I could ask you
the same question. sir.

506
00:46:43.003 --> 00:46:44.838
if I could even call you that.

507
00:46:44.972 --> 00:46:46.840
You either join in or
you get the fuck out.

508
00:46:48.008 --> 00:46:49.544
Join in what?

509
00:46:52.379 --> 00:46:53.548
I said no!

510
00:46:54.982 --> 00:46:56.216
Ma'am. you
need to get warm.

511
00:46:56.350 --> 00:46:57.318
You're sick.

512
00:46:57.451 --> 00:46:58.553
Come with me.

513
00:47:00.254 --> 00:47:02.724
Never interrupt a man
in the middle of a screw.

514
00:47:06.093 --> 00:47:09.463
That
whore belongs to me!

515
00:47:19.139 --> 00:47:20.709
